# Additional configuration for erlinit
#
# To override the settings in this file, see
# https://hexdocs.pm/nerves/advanced-configuration.html#overriding-erlinit-config-from-mix-config.
#

# Turn on the debug prints
#-v

# Specify where erlinit should send the IEx prompt. Only one may be enabled at
# a time.
-c ttyS0  # UART0 on the PH pins (internal test pads)
#-c ttyGS0  # USB gadget serial -- see README, requires the app to set up the
            # gadget since nothing configures USB configfs at boot.

# If more than one tty are available, always warn if the user is looking at the
# wrong one. This matters more here than on a dev board: the RG40XXV has no pin
# header, so it is easy to be attached to the wrong console.
--warn-unused-tty

# Use nbtty to improve terminal handling on serial ports.
-s "/usr/bin/nbtty"

# Specify the user and group IDs for the Erlang VM
#--uid 100
#--gid 200

# Uncomment to ensure that the system clock is set to at least the Nerves
# System's build date/time. If you enable this, you'll still need to use NTP or
# another mechanism to set the clock, but it won't be decades off.
#--update-clock

# Uncomment to hang the board rather than rebooting when Erlang exits
# NOTE: Do not enable on production boards
#--hang-on-exit

# Change the graceful shutdown time. If 10 seconds isn't long enough between
# calling "poweroff", "reboot", or "halt" and :init.stop/0 stopping all OTP
# applications, enable this option with a new timeout in milliseconds.
#--graceful-shutdown-timeout 15000

# Optionally run a program if the Erlang VM exits
#--run-on-exit /bin/sh

# Nothing here brings up the display, and nothing here should.
#
# This file used to carry
#
#     --pre-run-exec /sbin/modprobe panel-mipi
#
# because the panel driver was a module. It is built in now, along with the
# rest of the sun4i stack, and its description is linked into the kernel image
# by CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE -- so the screen is alive before init runs and there
# is no module left to load. Re-adding that line only logs an error.
#
# The reason it was ever a module is worth keeping, because it looks like an
# argument for putting it back: a built-in driver probes before any filesystem
# is mounted, so request_firmware() could not reach /lib/firmware and the first
# built-in attempt failed with -2. Embedding the blob is what answers that, not
# loading the driver later. docs/display.md has the whole account.
#
# One fact from that period still holds and is still a trap: the panel cannot
# autoload. The SPI core derives the modalias from the panel's first compatible
# string ("spi:rg40xx-v2-panel") while the driver advertises
# "panel-mipi-dpi-spi", so a modular panel is a module nothing loads. If the
# build ever demotes CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_MIPI back to =m -- which Kconfig will do
# silently the moment CONFIG_DRM is =m -- the symptom is a blank screen with no
# error: every other display driver still binds and /sys/class/backlight still
# appears, but there is no /sys/class/drm/card0, because sun4i's component
# master cannot complete without the panel. tools/gen-kernel-defconfig.sh
# asserts against exactly that.

# Enable UTF-8 filename handling in Erlang and custom inet configuration
-e LANG=en_US.UTF-8;LANGUAGE=en;ERL_INETRC=/etc/erl_inetrc

# Enable crash dumps (set ERL_CRASH_DUMP_SECONDS=0 to disable)
-e ERL_CRASH_DUMP=/root/erl_crash.dump;ERL_CRASH_DUMP_SECONDS=5

# Mount the application partition (run "man fstab" for field names)
# NOTE: This must match the location in the fwup.conf. If it doesn't the system
#       will probably still work fine, but you won't get shell history since
#       shoehorn/nerves_runtime can't mount the application filesystem before
#       the history is loaded. If this mount fails due to corruption, etc.,
#       nerves_runtime will auto-format it. Your applications will need to handle
#       initializing any expected files and folders.
#
# nodiscard: f2fs turns discard on by default when the device claims to
# support it, and this card times out on erase (mmc_erase: group start error
# -110). Left alone, an app-level watchdog found the filesystem wedge solid
# after the discards piled up (mmcblk0p4 stopped answering reads
# mid-session). This is a fstab-style options field (5th, after the mount
# flags), not a mount flag itself -- erlinit only recognizes a fixed set of
# flag names and silently drops anything else, so nodiscard has to go here
# to take effect.
#
# The application already remounts nodiscard once Elixir is up
# (MayonnaiOS.AppPartition), because that ships without a rebuild -- its
# moduledoc says outright that this file is "the right place" once someone is
# rebuilding anyway. Doing it here just closes the window before that
# remount runs, in case the timeout wedges the filesystem that early.
-m /dev/mmcblk0p4:/root:f2fs:nodev:nodiscard

# Erlang release search path
-r /srv/erlang

# Assign a hostname of the form "nerves-<last 8 chars of the serial number>".
# See /etc/boardid.config for locating the serial number.
-d /usr/bin/boardid
-n nerves-%-.8s

# If using shoehorn (https://github.com/nerves-project/shoehorn), start the
# shoehorn OTP release up first. If shoehorn isn't around, erlinit fails back
# to the main OTP release.
--boot shoehorn
